%T A399906 5,1,2,5,9,3,4,5,6,6,1,3,4,2,5,6,10,6,11,5,1,2,12,3,6,4,13,6,14,5,15,
%U A399906 1,3,4,2,5,6,7,7,16,6,8,8,1,2,6,3,4,7,8,7
%N A399906 Word representation of the precise greedy grasshopper infinite barrycade (recursively defined family of permutations of the positive integers having pairwise disjoint sets of partial sums).
%C A399906 A barrycade is a collection of rows whose sets of partial sums are pairwise disjoint. In the infinite version considered here, each row is a permutation of the positive integers.
%C A399906 Let G_phi = {phi1, phi2, ...} be the precise greedy grasshopper infinite barrycade defined by the construction of A399905, with every earlier row regarded in its entirety as an infinite permutation. For n >= 1, a(n)=r if n occurs as a partial sum in row phi_r.
%C A399906 The construction is break-free: every positive integer occurs as a partial sum in exactly one row. Hence a(n) is always positive and records which row of the barrycade has a partial sum at position n.
%C A399906 The spelling "barrycade" is due to Richard Guy, who used it instead of "barricade" in honor of Barry Cipra, who prompted him to study the problem.
%H A399906 M. Dębski, J. Grytczuk, P. Naroski, B. Pawlik, J. Przybyło and M. Śleszyńska-Nowak, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.18476">Finite and infinite barrycades</a>, arXiv:2609.18476 [math.CO], 2026.
%F A399906 a(n)=r if n belongs to S(phi_r), where S(phi_r) is the set of partial sums of row phi_r.
%F A399906 A399905(r) = min { n >= 1 : a(n)=r }.
%t A399906 A399906[n_] := Module[{u,s,p,init,step,extend,covered,r=1,a=ConstantArray[0,n]},covered[0,_]=False;covered[j_,x_]:=AnyTrue[Range[j],(init[#];extend[#,x];MemberQ[p[#],x])&];init[j_]:=If[!ValueQ[s[j]],Module[{m=1},While[covered[j-1,m],m++];u[j]={m};s[j]=m;p[j]={m}]];step[j_]:=Module[{k=1,q=1},While[MemberQ[u[j],k],k++];If[!covered[j-1,s[j]+k],AppendTo[u[j],k];s[j]+=k;AppendTo[p[j],s[j]],While[MemberQ[u[j],q]||q==k||covered[j-1,s[j]+q]||covered[j-1,s[j]+q+k],q++];Scan[(AppendTo[u[j],#];s[j]+=#;AppendTo[p[j],s[j]])&,{q,k}]]];extend[j_,x_]:=(init[j];While[s[j]<x,step[j]]);While[MemberQ[a,0],init[r];extend[r,n];Scan[If[#<=n,a[[#]]=r]&,p[r]];r++];a]
%Y A399906 Cf. A399897-A399909 for other sequences arising from infinite barrycade constructions.
%K A399906 nonn,new
%O A399906 1,2
%A A399906 _Bartlomiej Pawlik_, Sep 23 2026
